Fixed. The error was in test_background_spawn_and_collect (src/commands_spawn.rs:1904): try_collect now returns a 3-tuple including the new Option<SpawnHandoff> handoff field, but the test still destructured a 2-tuple.

The fix updates the destructuring and asserts the handoff is None (a plain complete() without worktree changes has no handoff):

```rust
let (task, result, handoff) = collected.unwrap();
assert_eq!(task, "bg task");
assert_eq!(result, "bg result");
assert!(handoff.is_none());
```

Verified: cargo fmt, cargo build, cargo test (4100 + 88 passed, 0 failed), and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` all pass.
